@node Authentication (1)
@section Authentication

@vindex spofy-client-id
@vindex spofy-client-secret
@vindex spofy-redirect-port
@vindex spofy-token-file

The user option @code{spofy-client-id} holds the Client ID of your registered Spotify application.  It defaults to @code{nil}.  Without this value, Spofy cannot communicate with the Spotify API@.  Obtain it from the Spotify Developer Dashboard (@ref{Getting started}). @*

The user option @code{spofy-client-secret} holds the Client Secret of your registered Spotify application.  It defaults to @code{nil}.  Like the client ID, this is required for the OAuth2 token exchange. @*

The user option @code{spofy-redirect-port} controls the port on which Spofy's temporary OAuth2 callback server listens.  It defaults to @code{8080}.  Change this if port 8080 is already in use on your machine.  The redirect URI registered in the Spotify Developer Dashboard must match the port you configure here. @*

The user option @code{spofy-token-file} specifies where Spofy stores OAuth tokens and the access-token expiry time.  It defaults to @samp{spofy-tokens.el} in the user Emacs directory.  Tokens are stored as a Lisp alist and the file is written with restrictive permissions (mode 600) so that only the file owner can read it.  For additional security, use a @samp{.gpg} extension (e.g. @samp{spofy-tokens.el.gpg}) to have Emacs encrypt the file automatically via EasyPG; this requires a configured GPG key.  When writing to a @samp{.gpg} file, Spofy binds @code{epa-file-select-keys} to @code{silent} to suppress the interactive GPG recipient selection dialog. @*

@node Playback
@section Playback

@vindex spofy-poll-interval
@vindex spofy-seek-seconds
@vindex spofy-volume-step
The user option @code{spofy-poll-interval} sets the number of seconds between player state polls.  It defaults to @code{5}.  Lower values make the UI more responsive to changes (e.g. track transitions) at the cost of more API requests.  The Spotify API does not provide push notifications, so polling is the only way to detect state changes. @*

The user option @code{spofy-seek-seconds} controls how many seconds @code{spofy-seek-forward} and @code{spofy-seek-backward} jump.  It defaults to @code{10}. @*

The user option @code{spofy-volume-step} sets the percentage increment for @code{spofy-volume-up} and @code{spofy-volume-down}.  It defaults to @code{5}.  Valid volume values range from 0 to 100. @*

@node Mode-line
@section Mode-line

@vindex spofy-mode-line-format
@vindex spofy-mode-line-max-length
@vindex spofy-mode-line-separator

The user option @code{spofy-mode-line-format} is a format string that controls what the mode-line segment displays.  It defaults to @code{"▶ %t — %a"}.  The following specifiers are available: @*

@multitable {aaaaaaaaa} {aaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaa}
@headitem Specifier
@tab Meaning
@item @samp{%t}
@tab Track name
@item @samp{%a}
@tab Artist name
@item @samp{%b}
@tab Album name
@item @samp{%p}
@tab Play/pause icon (⏸ when playing, ▶ when paused)
@item @samp{%s}
@tab Shuffle indicator (⇌ when on, empty when off)
@item @samp{%r}
@tab Repeat indicator (↻ for context, ↻₁ for track, empty)
@end multitable

The user option @code{spofy-mode-line-max-length} sets the maximum character length of the mode-line string.  It defaults to @code{40}.  Longer strings are silently truncated.  Increase this if you have a wide frame and want to see more of the track and artist names. @*

The user option @code{spofy-mode-line-separator} is the string inserted before the Spofy segment in the mode line.  It defaults to a single space. @*

@node Tab-bar
@section Tab-bar

@vindex spofy-tab-bar-format
@vindex spofy-tab-bar-progress-width
@vindex spofy-tab-bar-max-length
@vindex spofy-tab-bar-alignment

The user option @code{spofy-tab-bar-format} is a format string that controls what the tab-bar segment displays.  It defaults to @code{"%t %a %s%r %G"}, which shows the track and artist, shuffle and repeat indicators, and a progress bar.  The same format specifiers as @code{spofy-mode-line-format} are supported (@ref{Mode-line}), plus two additional specifiers: @samp{%G} inserts a progress bar, and @samp{%T} inserts the timestamps (e.g. ``1:23 / 3:45''). @*

The user option @code{spofy-tab-bar-progress-width} sets the width in characters of the progress bar in the tab bar.  It defaults to @code{15}.  This option is only relevant when the format string contains @samp{%G}. @*

The user option @code{spofy-tab-bar-max-length} sets the maximum character length of the tab-bar string.  It defaults to @code{50}.  Longer strings are silently truncated.  Set it to @code{nil} to disable truncation entirely. @*

The user option @code{spofy-tab-bar-alignment} controls whether the Spofy segment appears on the left or right side of the tab bar.  It accepts the symbols @code{left} (default) and @code{right}.  When set to @code{left}, the segment is inserted before any @code{tab-bar-format-align-right} entry, keeping it on the left side.  When set to @code{right}, the segment is placed after @code{tab-bar-format-align-right}, inserting that alignment entry automatically if it is not already present.  Set this option before enabling @code{spofy-tab-bar-mode} (@ref{Tab-bar display}). @*

@node Global key and mode-line activation
@section Global key and mode-line activation

@vindex spofy-global-key
@vindex spofy-enable-mode-line
@vindex spofy-enable-tab-bar
@vindex spofy-dashboard-album-art
@vindex spofy-dashboard-sections

The user option @code{spofy-global-key} sets the prefix key that @code{spofy-global-mode} binds to @code{spofy-menu}.  It defaults to @code{"C-c s"}.  Change this if the default conflicts with other bindings. @*

The user option @code{spofy-enable-mode-line} controls whether @code{spofy-global-mode} automatically enables @code{spofy-mode-line-mode}.  It defaults to @code{t}.  Set it to @code{nil} if you prefer a clean mode line and want to access now-playing information only through the dashboard or transient popup. @*

The user option @code{spofy-enable-tab-bar} controls whether @code{spofy-global-mode} automatically enables @code{spofy-tab-bar-mode}.  It defaults to @code{nil}.  Set it to @code{t} to display the currently playing track in the tab bar (@ref{Tab-bar display}). @*

The two display modes are mutually exclusive: when @code{spofy-enable-tab-bar} is non-nil, it takes precedence and the mode-line display is not enabled, regardless of @code{spofy-enable-mode-line}.  This avoids duplication because Emacs renders @code{global-mode-string} (where the mode-line segment lives) in the tab bar via @code{tab-bar-format-global}, which would otherwise cause the track information to appear twice. @*

The user option @code{spofy-dashboard-sections} controls which sections appear on the dashboard and in what order.  It defaults to @code{(recently-played playlists)}.  Each element is a symbol naming a section.  Available sections: @*

@table @asis
@item @code{recently-played}
Last 10 tracks played. @*
@item @code{playlists}
First 10 user playlists. @*
@item @code{top-tracks-short}
Top tracks from the last 4 weeks. @*
@item @code{top-tracks-medium}
Top tracks from the last 6 months. @*
@item @code{top-tracks-long}
Top tracks from the last year. @*
@item @code{top-artists-short}
Top artists from the last 4 weeks. @*
@item @code{top-artists-medium}
Top artists from the last 6 months. @*
@item @code{top-artists-long}
Top artists from the last year. @*
@item @code{new-releases}
New album releases (not personalized). @*
@end table

The user option @code{spofy-dashboard-album-art} controls whether album artwork is displayed in the now-playing section.  It defaults to @code{t}.  When enabled, the album cover appears between the track information (track, artist, album) and the player controls (progress bar, shuffle/repeat state).  Album art is fetched asynchronously from the Spotify API and cached on disk under @samp{XDG_CACHE_HOME/spofy/album-art/} (defaulting to @samp{~/.cache/spofy/album-art/}).  The image updates automatically when the track changes.  This option has no effect in terminal frames, since Emacs cannot display images there. @*

The now-playing section always appears at the top regardless of this option.  Each section is fetched asynchronously and includes a ``View all'' link that opens a full tabulated-list buffer.  Track and artist names in every section are truncated to the window width with a fade-out gradient when they would otherwise overflow. @*

@node Column widths
@section Column widths

@vindex spofy-columns
@findex spofy-ui-col
@findex spofy-ui-set-format
@findex spofy-ui-compute-format

Variable-width columns are sized dynamically so that all columns together fill the window.  The user option @code{spofy-columns} controls the proportional weights of these columns.  Each entry maps a view symbol to a list of weights; columns are allocated window space in proportion to their weight.  Fixed-width columns such as indicators, duration, year, and track counts are not affected.  Column widths are recomputed automatically when the window is resized.  The default weights are: @*

@multitable {aaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaa} {aaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaa}
@headitem View
@tab Columns (weights)
@item @samp{library-track}
@tab Name (35), Artist(s) (25), Album (25)
@item @samp{library-album}
@tab Name (35), Artist(s) (25)
@item @samp{search-track}
@tab Name (35), Artist(s) (25), Album (25)
@item @samp{search-album}
@tab Name (35), Artist(s) (25)
@item @samp{search-artist}
@tab Name (35), Genres (30)
@item @samp{search-playlist}
@tab Name (35), Owner (20)
@item @samp{album-track}
@tab Name (40), Artist(s) (25)
@item @samp{artist-album}
@tab Name (40)
@item @samp{artist-top-track}
@tab Name (35), Album (25)
@item @samp{playlist-track}
@tab Name (30), Artist(s) (20), Album (20)
@item @samp{playlist-list}
@tab Name (35), Owner (20)
@end multitable

The function @code{spofy-ui-compute-format} takes a view symbol and a list of column specs, where each spec is @samp{(NAME WIDTH SORT . PROPS)}.  When WIDTH is the keyword @samp{:flex}, the column width is computed proportionally from @code{spofy-columns}.  The convenience function @code{spofy-ui-set-format} calls @code{spofy-ui-compute-format} and stores the recipe so that column widths are recomputed on window resize.  The function @code{spofy-ui-col} returns the computed width for a given view and flex column index. @*

