The command @code{spofy-playlist-add-track} adds a track to a playlist.  When called interactively, it attempts to get the track URI from the entity at point, then presents the user's playlists in @code{completing-read} for target selection.  This command is available from search results (@ref{Navigating search results}), library views (@ref{Library management}), and browse views. @*

The command @code{spofy-playlist-remove-track} removes the track at point from the current playlist.  It only works in playlist detail buffers (@ref{Playlist detail view}). @*

The command @code{spofy-playlist-reorder} moves the track at point to a new position within the playlist.  It prompts for the target position (1-indexed for the user interface, converted internally to the 0-indexed API format). @*

The command @code{spofy-playlist-set-public} toggles the public/private visibility of the playlist at point. @*

The command @code{spofy-follow-playlist} prompts for a playlist ID or URI and follows it.  The command @code{spofy-unfollow-playlist} unfollows the playlist at point (equivalent to @code{spofy-delete-playlist}). @*

